import{_ as t,c as a,o as r,ag as n}from"./chunks/framework.Vyheyqg9.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Build AI Apps — JavaScript First","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"applied-ai/index.md","filePath":"applied-ai/index.md"}'),i={name:"applied-ai/index.md"};function o(s,e,d,l,p,h){return r(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="build-ai-apps-—-javascript-first" tabindex="-1">Build AI Apps — JavaScript First <a class="header-anchor" href="#build-ai-apps-—-javascript-first" aria-label="Permalink to “Build AI Apps — JavaScript First”">​</a></h1><p>Start here if you know some JavaScript but are new to AI development. Build a chatbot inside a web app, let it use a checked tool, teach it to answer from your notes, and expose those notes through your own MCP server. Python is an optional continuation, not an entrance requirement.</p><p>Want help <strong>using AI to fix bugs, develop features and prepare PRs</strong>? Follow <a href="./../ai-assisted-engineering/">AI for Software Development</a> alongside this path. That course teaches your development process; this one teaches the software you build.</p><h2 id="start-with-one-small-project" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">1 </span>Start with one small project <a class="header-anchor" href="#start-with-one-small-project" aria-label="Permalink to “1 Start with one small project”">​</a></h2><p>The continuing project is a <strong>learning-notes assistant</strong> using three public synthetic notes. Begin in offline simulation mode: no account, key or paid model is required. A simulation teaches request flow and UI behavior; it cannot demonstrate model intelligence or quality. Try a real provider only after understanding the server boundary and recording a small experiment budget.</p><p><strong>Your first session:</strong> read <a href="./javascript/orientation.html">0. Understand the pieces</a>, run the console in <a href="./javascript/first-call.html">1. First call</a>, ask one question, reset the conversation and exit. Do not install a graph framework or study every Python chapter first.</p><h2 id="follow-this-sequence" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">2 </span>Follow this sequence <a class="header-anchor" href="#follow-this-sequence" aria-label="Permalink to “2 Follow this sequence”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Learn and build</th><th>Done when you can…</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0</td><td><a href="./javascript/orientation.html">Understand the pieces</a></td><td>Explain model, application, prompt, context, tool, workflow, agent, RAG and MCP in your own words</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td><a href="./javascript/first-call.html">First request and console chat</a></td><td>Run offline, locate the provider boundary and explain where the key belongs</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><a href="./javascript/chatbot.html">Chatbot inside a web app</a></td><td>Trace browser→server→model, handle failure, retain bounded history and stop a request</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><a href="./javascript/structured-output.html">Reliable structured output</a></td><td>Validate a result and reject a fabricated quote</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><a href="./javascript/tools-workflows.html">Tools and workflows</a></td><td>Dispatch only an allowed read and prepare a proposal without executing it</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><a href="./javascript/rag.html">RAG from your notes</a></td><td>Compare lexical and semantic retrieval, cite sources and decline unsupported answers</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><a href="./javascript/mcp.html">Build an MCP server</a></td><td>Discover and call an SDK tool, read a resource and retrieve a prompt</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><a href="./javascript/stateful-workflows.html">Stateful graph workflows</a></td><td>Branch, interrupt and resume a graph; distinguish RAM from durable state</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><a href="./javascript/extensions.html">Choose your next extension</a></td><td>Choose Python, hosted storage, n8n, multimedia or A2A for a concrete need</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Use the <a href="./../practice/applied-ai/javascript-assistant.html">JavaScript practice milestones</a> for independent implementation. The <a href="./../workbench/applied-ai/javascript/">starter workbench</a> is a worked reference, not a completed learner submission. Each lesson separates supplied behavior from the extension you implement.</p><h2 id="keep-the-deeper-material" tabindex="-1"><span class="hub-section-number">3 </span>Keep the deeper material <a class="header-anchor" href="#keep-the-deeper-material" aria-label="Permalink to “3 Keep the deeper material”">​</a></h2><p>The existing lessons and URLs remain available. Visit them when a project reaches the relevant problem:</p><ul><li><a href="./shared/">Shared foundations</a>: model schemas, budgets, security, evaluation and diagnostics.</li><li><a href="./rag/">RAG engineering</a>: provenance, retrieval quality, access control and index lifecycle.</li><li><a href="./workflows/">Workflow engineering</a>: approvals, durable recovery, receipts and controlled autonomy.</li><li><a href="./n8n/">n8n</a>: visual automation and service integration.</li><li><a href="./../python-for-ai/">Python for AI — Optional Deep Dive</a>: language prerequisites and existing detailed implementations.</li></ul><p>The <a href="./coverage-map.html">coverage map</a> distinguishes beginner JavaScript examples, deeper Python mechanisms and integrations still left to the learner. Reading, a mock response and passing reference checks are different observations; none completes your independent project.</p>',13)])])}const m=t(i,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
